# Root build context — keep the image a build of the SOURCE, not the machine.
# Deliberately NOT ignored: scripts/ (fleet skills + chassis template ship into
# the runtime image). apps/ is not ignored either, though no build step reads it
# any more: an instance compiles its installed apps at runtime, from
# TALARIA_APPS_DIR (see the Dockerfile's note on the build stage's COPY).

.git
.git/**
**/.git
.github

node_modules
**/node_modules
# …except an app's own: apps are self-contained codebases (apps/README.md) —
# their node_modules are source, not something this image rebuilds (ui/ and
# mcp/ get fresh installs; apps/ don't).
!apps/*/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage

# Rust build output — a devbox's compiled artifacts never enter a context.
# The api compiles exactly once, in CI (api/package.Dockerfile, published by
# api-package.yml); the root Dockerfile doesn't compile it at all, it
# consumes the published package image.
api/target

# Instance state — never bake a machine's data or credentials into a layer.
fleet
stack
logs
**/.uploads
# The app platform's dev state: app databases (pg/ is the container user's,
# db.env is a password) and compiled app builds.
app-data
app-builds
ui/.env*
# The legacy SearXNG settings file an old checkout may still hold (it carries
# a secret_key; see .gitignore) — never part of a local build context.
docker/searxng/settings.local.yml
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# Not part of any build.
docs
playground
.claude
.inspect
cli
*.md
LICENSE
